{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1397633-wolf-blooded-monstrosities","id":1397633,"title":"Wolf-Blooded Monstrosities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-19T23:51:59-07:00","id":1397633,"title":"Wolf-Blooded Monstrosities","content":"Werewolf: The Forsaken 2e, Appendix One: Wolf-Blooded. Where Are You Running?<br /> This question provides 5 possibilities; Pack Loyalty, Isolation, Monstrosity, a Vigil, &amp; the Change. Now, 4 of these answers are straightforward, I get what they're about. We're here to talk about the fifth one. We're here to talk about Monstrosities &amp; more specifically, what they could look like.<br /> <br /> The Pack of Low Wolves: a bunch of Wolf-Blooded's gather, their strength bleeding into one another. The individual wolf-blooded can psychically communicate via a sort of pack mentality. Each one of them also gains the ability to use the Tells of any of the other members in the group. However, this is not normal, not natural, not right. The pack forging/joining causes each individual wolf-blooded to lose any sense of human morality, mentally becoming savage lupine beasts that think more like spirits than anything of the flesh. This affliction can only affect wolf-blooded that are not attached to an Uratha pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T23:28:13-07:00","id":1398134,"title":"","content":"Tell Render<br /> This is effectively the first variety of Wolf-Blooded Monstrosity I ever developed, though I was more aiming for a single villain who just happened to be wolf-blooded.<br /> The idea behind the Tell Render is that they are a wolf-blooded who has used a certain ritual at least once. This ritual allows a wolf-blooded to steal the Tell of another wolf-blooded, in it's entirety. The ritual is a very visceral one &amp; I imagine that eaten the heart of the victim wolf-blooded would be part of the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T23:53:32-07:00","id":1398138,"title":"","content":"I was thinking that perhaps certain Tyrants could find a way to reincarnate within the bodies of wolf-blooded they rule over, effectively forcing them through the First Change. Their Auspice would be left behind, though, leaving them weakened unless they were Pure beforehand. A rite probably makes the most sense for how to prime wolf-blooded to be the Tyrant's potential receptacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T23:00:02-07:00","id":1398949,"title":"","content":"Tell Warping: a rare affliction affecting wolf-bloodeds. It requires low morality &amp; the primary results are causing a strengthening &amp; warping of Tells, &amp; a focus on Vice, emphasizing the darker parts of the personality. Possibilities for various Tell Warpings follow: <br /> \u25cf Anger Issues: This warped suffers from berserker madness with multiple buttons to set them off. The results of the berserker madness are enhanced strength, indiscriminately killing people, &amp; the ability to ignore pain &amp; injuries.<br /> \u25cf Evil Eye: This warped can inflict various, vicious curses with a look.<br /> \u25cf Phantom Pack: This warped is the alpha of a pack of spectral wolves, which they can allow to temporarily, physically manifest. The wolves emanate an aura of fear that affects anyone the alpha wants it to.<br /> \u25cf Skinner: This warped can remove the skin from a person &amp; wear it, taking on not only the person's appearance but also their skills &amp; attributes. They can access memories &amp; imitate personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T16:36:42-07:00","id":1400204,"title":"","content":"Garwulf: Garwulves were once just wolf-blooded with Tells that leaned towards the flesh side of their heritage. Wounded soul. They can infect people, turning them into &quot;Geralphi&quot; &amp; these infected people then turn to the one who infected them as alpha. The Garwulf can command a number of people, but if they go over their maximum number they start finding it difficult to command these infected people. Any infected people will normally turn back to normal humans when the &quot;master&quot; is killed, however some may become wolf-blooded.<br /> \u25cf Geralphus (plural Geralphi): enhanced strength. Shapeshifting (human, near-wolf). Blind loyalty. Instinctively know in which direction their &quot;master&quot; is. Regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T21:10:32-08:00","id":1439589,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I last posted on this thread. But I don't think it's been long enough that it qualifies as thread necromancy.<br /> Fingers crossed that I'm correct about that.<br /> I have six more varieties of wolf-blooded monstrosities to share.<br /> <br /> Geryo Blessed, Idigam Bound, Moonlight Soldier, Sunlight Sworn. In the case of these four I have nothing but names. I was unable to come up with any idea for how they would operate. Sorry about that. As is, they can used as the basis for unsettling rumors to drop into the setting. Or some mechanics could be developed, a theory on how they come to be, &amp; they could be introduced to your game.<br /> <br /> Plant Touched. These guys are in pretty much the same boat as the four just above. They're inspired by the Ursuma from LostLight's Strange Changes supplement. No mechanics developed, but I think that if Plant Touched are encountered, then there's an Ursuma in the area.<br /> <br /> The Wolf Eaters: these guys have learned a rite which enables them to assume many of an uratha's abilities (barring Gifts, rites, Auspice benefits, &amp; fetish &amp; talen use). The rite requires the consumption of uratha flesh.<br /> The effects of the rite are temporary, thus must be performed with some regularity to retain the power. Over time, this distorts the wolf-blooded, to the point where if they stop performing the rite for long enough that the stolen power fades away, their bodies will start to literally break down.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> I doubt I'm going to come up with any more ideas to slot under the umbrella of wolf-blooded monstrosities, so this looks like the last post on this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}